  "body": "There's nothing helpful in the logs:\r\n```\r\n2018-12-07 05:41:28,658 - synapse.access.http.8008 - 233 - INFO - GET-15283 - ::ffff:127.0.0.1 - 8008 - Received request: GET /_matrix/client/r0/sync?filter=1&timeout=30000&since=s4590_70910_39_422_635_9_1_444_5\r\n2018-12-07 05:41:28,659 - synapse.api.auth - 500 - WARNING - GET-15283 - Unrecognised access token - not in store.\r\n2018-12-07 05:41:28,659 - synapse.http.server - 85 - INFO - GET-15283 - <SynapseRequest at 0x7f629e0d1560 method=u'GET' uri=u'/_matrix/client/r0/sync?filter=1&timeout=30000&since=s4590_70910_39_422_635_9_1_444_5' clientproto=u'HTTP/1.0' site=8008> SynapseError: 401 - Unrecognised access token.\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt was syncing fine up until this point and was operating normally. The account in question survived less than 15-30 minutes and shows no indication of being logged out elsewhere. Although it may not be relevant, the account was a guest account.\r\n\r\nSynapse is running on the latest develop (as of writing) and on python 2, installed via pip.",
